            <ArticleTitle>Acute abdomen due to placenta percreta.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>335-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Placenta percreta is a rare but serious complication of pregnancy, usually presenting itself in the third trimester. The incidence of fetal death and maternal mortality is high. We report a case presenting as an acute abdomen, due to haemoperitoneum at 33 weeks of pregnancy. Incidence, etiology, diagnosis and treatment are discussed, and the literature is reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
